                <pb facs="0741" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00/1158: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >South</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-28T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                                1925—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>26. The Minister for Foreign Affairs assures me Indians will not be attacked
                    unless they renew hostilities. Seizure of boats a precautionary measure which
                    can be abandoned if it causes difficulties.</p>
                <p>Señor Alfaro believes that public opinion will demand thorough investigation of
                    Marsh’s activities but it is disposed to give him benefit of all favorable
                    evidence. Justice of the Supreme Court leaving tonight for Carti to make this
                    investigation and hear evidence of Indians.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">South</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
